\i\f77\fs20\cf2\insrsid14899619  HYPERLINK "http://www.sichosinenglish.org/books/upsherinish/02.htm" \\l "t11" }}{\fldrslt {\rtlch \ai\af0\afs20 \ltrch \cs16\i\f77\fs20\ul\cf6\insrsid14899619 Back to text}}}{\rtlch \ai\af0\afs20 \ltrch 
\i\f77\fs20\cf2\insrsid14899619 {\*\bkmkend n11}) A four-cornered garment with tassels worn to fulfill the Biblical command (Numbers 15:38): "Make tassels on the corners of your garments."
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\ltrpar \rtlch \ai\af0\afs20\alang1025 \ltrch \i\f77\fs20\cf2\insrsid14899619 \hich\af77\dbch\af0\loch\f77 12.\tab}}\pard \ltrpar\ql \fi-360\li720\ri0\sb100\sa100\sbauto1\saauto1\widctlpar
\jclisttab\tx720\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\ls12\adjustright\rin0\lin720\itap0\pararsid14899619 {\rtlch \ai\af0\afs20 \ltrch \i\f77\fs20\cf2\insrsid14899619 ({\*\bkmkstart n12}}{\field\fldedit{\*\fldinst {\rtlch \ai\af0\afs20 \ltrch 
\i\f77\fs20\cf2\insrsid14899619  HYPERLINK "http://www.sichosinenglish.org/books/upsherinish/02.htm" \\l "t12" }}{\fldrslt {\rtlch \ai\af0\afs20 \ltrch \cs16\i\f77\fs20\ul\cf6\insrsid14899619 Back to text}}}{\rtlch \ai\af0\afs20 \ltrch 
\i\f77\fs20\cf2\insrsid14899619 {\*\bkmkend n12}) I.e., as stated on p. 28, a boy
 may be trained to wear a yarmulka and tzitzis beforehand. At that age, however, a child is often too immature to appreciate what is doing, and perhaps even unable to control his bodily functions. Hence these garments are not worn at all times. From the u
psherinish onward, by contrast, children should be trained to wear these garments continuously.
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\ltrpar \rtlch \ai\af0\afs20\alang1025 \ltrch \i\f77\fs20\cf2\insrsid14899619 \hich\af77\dbch\af0\loch\f77 13.\tab}}\pard \ltrpar\ql \fi-360\li720\ri0\sb100\sa100\sbauto1\saauto1\widctlpar
