\i\f77\fs20\cf2\insrsid14899619 {\*\bkmkend n31}) In Kuntres Upsherinish, Rabbi 
Y.Y. Simon quotes advice the Rebbe gave a person who had cut his child's hair before the age of three, because that person had not appreciated the importance of this custom at that time. The Rebbe advised allowing the child's hair to grow untouched for a 
time and then holding the haircut together with a celebration. In this way, although the spiritual connection with the child's third birthday would be lacking, the child would gain the educational benefits.
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\ltrpar \rtlch \ai\af0\afs20\alang1025 \ltrch \i\f77\fs20\cf2\insrsid14899619 \hich\af77\dbch\af0\loch\f77 32.\tab}}\pard \ltrpar\ql \fi-360\li720\ri0\sb100\sa100\sbauto1\saauto1\widctlpar
