\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid14899619 {\rtlch \ab\af1\afs27 \ltrch \b\f1\fs27\cf2\insrsid14899619 What Is Done?
\par 
\par }{\rtlch \af0\afs20 \ltrch \f77\fs20\insrsid14899619 As mentioned, it is customary to hold - or at least start - the upsherinish in a holy setting, in a synagogue or a house of study. Both the mother and 
father should be present at the upsherinish. In addition, relatives and friends of the family are invited to participate, for it is customary to hold the celebration with many people, recalling the verse: }{\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch 
\f77\fs15\insrsid14899619 [{\*\bkmkstart t37}}{\field\fldedit{\*\fldinst {\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \f77\fs15\insrsid14899619  HYPERLINK "http://www.sichosinenglish.org/books/upsherinish/03.htm" \\l "n37" }}{\fldrslt {\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch 
\cs16\f77\fs15\ul\cf2\insrsid14899619 37}}}{\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \f77\fs15\insrsid14899619 {\*\bkmkend t37}]}{\rtlch \af0\afs20 \ltrch \f77\fs20\insrsid14899619  "The glory of the King is among the multitude of people."}{\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch 
\f77\fs15\insrsid14899619 [{\*\bkmkstart t38}}{\field\fldedit{\*\fldinst {\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \f77\fs15\insrsid14899619  HYPERLINK "http://www.sichosinenglish.org/books/upsherinish/03.htm" \\l "n38" }}{\fldrslt {\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch 
\cs16\f77\fs15\ul\cf2\insrsid14899619 38}}}{\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \f77\fs15\insrsid14899619 {\*\bkmkend t38}]}{\rtlch \af0 \ltrch \insrsid14899619 
\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\s15\ql \li0\ri0\sb100\sa100\sbauto1\saauto1\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid14899619 \rtlch \af0\afs24\alang1025 \ltrch \fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch \af0\afs20 
\ltrch \f77\fs20\insrsid14899619 The child should wear tzitzis for this ceremony.}{\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \f77\fs15\insrsid14899619 [{\*\bkmkstart t39}}{\field\fldedit{\*\fldinst {\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \f77\fs15\insrsid14899619 
 HYPERLINK "http://www.sichosinenglish.org/books/upsherinish/03.htm" \\l "n39" }}{\fldrslt {\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \cs16\f77\fs15\ul\cf2\insrsid14899619 39}}}{\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \f77\fs15\insrsid14899619 {\*\bkmkend t39}]}{\rtlch \af0\afs20 
\ltrch \f77\fs20\insrsid14899619  A person of spiritual stature is asked to be the first to snip off a lock of the child's hair. On one occasion, }{\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \f77\fs15\insrsid14899619 [{\*\bkmkstart t40}}{\field\fldedit{\*\fldinst {\rtlch 
\af0\afs15 \ltrch \f77\fs15\insrsid14899619  HYPERLINK "http://www.sichosinenglish.org/books/upsherinish/03.htm" \\l "n40" }}{\fldrslt {\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \cs16\f77\fs15\ul\cf2\insrsid14899619 40}}}{\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch 
\f77\fs15\insrsid14899619 {\*\bkmkend t40}]}{\rtlch \af0\afs20 \ltrch \f77\fs20\insrsid14899619  th
e Rebbe advised that the first person to cut the hair should be a kohen, then a levi, and then, a yisrael. Afterwards, each of the people in attendance may be given a turn.}{\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \f77\fs15\insrsid14899619 [{\*\bkmkstart t41}}
{\field\fldedit{\*\fldinst {\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \f77\fs15\insrsid14899619  HYPERLINK "http://www.sichosinenglish.org/books/upsherinish/03.htm" \\l "n41" }}{\fldrslt {\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \cs16\f77\fs15\ul\cf2\insrsid14899619 41}}}{\rtlch 
\af0\afs15 \ltrch \f77\fs15\insrsid14899619 {\*\bkmkend t41}]}{\rtlch \af0 \ltrch \insrsid14899619 
\par }{\rtlch \af0\afs20 \ltrch \f77\fs20\insrsid14899619 
(It is not necessary to finish cutting the child's hair at the upsherinish. A portion can be cut off there and the remainder cut off at home or by a barber. One should not, however, employ a gentile barber for this purpose.}{\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch 
\f77\fs15\insrsid14899619 [{\*\bkmkstart t42}}{\field\fldedit{\*\fldinst {\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \f77\fs15\insrsid14899619  HYPERLINK "http://www.sichosinenglish.org/books/upsherinish/03.htm" \\l "n42" }}{\fldrslt {\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch 
\cs16\f77\fs15\ul\cf2\insrsid14899619 42}}}{\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \f77\fs15\insrsid14899619 {\*\bkmkend t42}]}{\rtlch \af0\afs20 \ltrch \f77\fs20\insrsid14899619 )}{\rtlch \af0 \ltrch \insrsid14899619 
\par }{\rtlch \af0\afs20 \ltrch \f77\fs20\insrsid14899619 The Rebbe would begin by cutting the hair near the peyos, close to the child's ear. The rationale appears that since the purpose of the custom is to train the child to observe the mitzvah of not shavi
ng his peyos, the cutting should begin there.}{\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \f77\fs15\insrsid14899619 [{\*\bkmkstart t43}}{\field\fldedit{\*\fldinst {\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \f77\fs15\insrsid14899619 
 HYPERLINK "http://www.sichosinenglish.org/books/upsherinish/03.htm" \\l "n43" }}{\fldrslt {\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \cs16\f77\fs15\ul\cf2\insrsid14899619 43}}}{\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \f77\fs15\insrsid14899619 {\*\bkmkend t43}]}{\rtlch \af0 \ltrch 
\insrsid14899619 
\par }{\rtlch \af0\afs20 \ltrch \f77\fs20\insrsid14899619 The hair should be collected and buried, rather than thrown in the garbage. The Minchas Elazar would weigh the hairs and give an equivalent amount of coins to charity.}{\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch 
\f77\fs15\insrsid14899619 [{\*\bkmkstart t44}}{\field\fldedit{\*\fldinst {\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \f77\fs15\insrsid14899619  HYPERLINK "http://www.sichosinenglish.org/books/upsherinish/03.htm" \\l "n44" }}{\fldrslt {\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch 
\cs16\f77\fs15\ul\cf2\insrsid14899619 44}}}{\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \f77\fs15\insrsid14899619 {\*\bkmkend t44}]}{\rtlch \af0 \ltrch \insrsid14899619 
\par }{\rtlch \af0\afs20 \ltrch \f77\fs20\insrsid14899619 Based on a letter from the Rebbe's father,}{\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \f77\fs15\insrsid14899619 [{\*\bkmkstart t45}}{\field\fldedit{\*\fldinst {\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \f77\fs15\insrsid14899619 
 HYPERLINK "http://www.sichosinenglish.org/books/upsherinish/03.htm" \\l "n45" }}{\fldrslt {\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \cs16\f77\fs15\ul\cf2\insrsid14899619 45}}}{\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \f77\fs15\insrsid14899619 {\*\bkmkend t45}]}{\rtlch \af0\afs20 
\ltrch \f77\fs20\insrsid14899619  there are many who follow the practice of giving the child whose hair is being cut money to give to tzedakah. In that letter, the Rebbe's father draws a parallel to the custom of giving Chanukah gelt.}{\rtlch \af0 \ltrch 
\insrsid14899619 
\par }{\rtlch \af0\afs20 \ltrch \f77\fs20\insrsid14899619 At the ceremony, the child whose hair is being cut shou
ld recite the verse Torah Tzivah. There are many who have the other children in attendance complete the recitation of the twelve pesukim selected by the Rebbe.}{\rtlch \af0 \ltrch \insrsid14899619 
\par }{\rtlch \af0\afs20 \ltrch \f77\fs20\insrsid14899619 Some mark the occasion with a celebratory feast. At the very least, pastry and L'Chayims}{\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \f77\fs15\insrsid14899619 [{\*\bkmkstart t46}}{\field\fldedit{\*\fldinst {\rtlch 
\af0\afs15 \ltrch \f77\fs15\insrsid14899619  HYPERLINK "http://www.sichosinenglish.org/books/upsherinish/03.htm" \\l "n46" }}{\fldrslt {\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \cs16\f77\fs15\ul\cf2\insrsid14899619 46}}}{\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch 
\f77\fs15\insrsid14899619 {\*\bkmkend t46}]}{\rtlch \af0\afs20 \ltrch \f77\fs20\insrsid14899619  should be served. The child should be given an opportunity to recite blessings. Many enhance the celebration with song and music.}{\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch 
\f77\fs15\insrsid14899619 [{\*\bkmkstart t47}}{\field\fldedit{\*\fldinst {\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \f77\fs15\insrsid14899619  HYPERLINK "http://www.sichosinenglish.org/books/upsherinish/03.htm" \\l "n47" }}{\fldrslt {\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch 
\cs16\f77\fs15\ul\cf2\insrsid14899619 47}}}{\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \f77\fs15\insrsid14899619 {\*\bkmkend t47}]}{\rtlch \af0 \ltrch \insrsid14899619 
\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\qc \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid14899619 \rtlch \af0\afs24\alang1025 \ltrch \fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\field\fldedit{\*\fldinst {\rtlch \af0\afs20 \ltrch 
