\i\f77\fs20\cf2\insrsid14899619  HYPERLINK "http://www.sichosinenglish.org/books/upsherinish/03.htm" \\l "t38" }}{\fldrslt {\rtlch \ai\af0\afs20 \ltrch \cs16\i\f77\fs20\ul\cf6\insrsid14899619 Back to text}}}{\rtlch \ai\af0\afs20 \ltrch 
\i\f77\fs20\cf2\insrsid14899619 {\*\bkmkend n38}) Shaarei Teshuvah 531:7.
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\ltrpar \rtlch \ai\af0\afs20\alang1025 \ltrch \i\f77\fs20\cf2\insrsid14899619 \hich\af77\dbch\af0\loch\f77 39.\tab}}\pard \ltrpar\ql \fi-360\li2160\ri0\sb100\sa100\sbauto1\saauto1\widctlpar
\jclisttab\tx720\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\ls39\adjustright\rin0\lin2160\itap0\pararsid14899619 {\rtlch \ai\af0\afs20 \ltrch \i\f77\fs20\cf2\insrsid14899619 ({\*\bkmkstart n39}}{\field\fldedit{\*\fldinst {\rtlch \ai\af0\afs20 \ltrch 
\i\f77\fs20\cf2\insrsid14899619  HYPERLINK "http://www.sichosinenglish.org/books/upsherinish/03.htm" \\l "t39" }}{\fldrslt {\rtlch \ai\af0\afs20 \ltrch \cs16\i\f77\fs20\ul\cf6\insrsid14899619 Back to text}}}{\rtlch \ai\af0\afs20 \ltrch 
\i\f77\fs20\cf2\insrsid14899619 {\*\bkmkend n39}) An association is drawn between this mitz
vah and this practice because locks of hair are also referred to as tzitzis. As mentioned on page 12, from the time of the upsherinish onward, a child should continue observing the mitzvah of tzitzis in a consistent manner.
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\ltrpar \rtlch \ai\af0\afs20\alang1025 \ltrch \i\f77\fs20\cf2\insrsid14899619 \hich\af77\dbch\af0\loch\f77 40.\tab}}\pard \ltrpar\ql \fi-360\li2160\ri0\sb100\sa100\sbauto1\saauto1\widctlpar
\jclisttab\tx720\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\ls40\adjustright\rin0\lin2160\itap0\pararsid14899619 {\rtlch \ai\af0\afs20 \ltrch \i\f77\fs20\cf2\insrsid14899619 ({\*\bkmkstart n40}}{\field\fldedit{\*\fldinst {\rtlch \ai\af0\afs20 \ltrch 
\i\f77\fs20\cf2\insrsid14899619  HYPERLINK "http://www.sichosinenglish.org/books/upsherinish/03.htm" \\l "t40" }}{\fldrslt {\rtlch \ai\af0\afs20 \ltrch \cs16\i\f77\fs20\ul\cf6\insrsid14899619 Back to text}}}{\rtlch \ai\af0\afs20 \ltrch 
\i\f77\fs20\cf2\insrsid14899619 {\*\bkmkend n40}) In a directive gi\ltrpar ven to Rabbi Yitzchak David Groner.
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\ltrpar \rtlch \ai\af0\afs20\alang1025 \ltrch \i\f77\fs20\cf2\insrsid14899619 \hich\af77\dbch\af0\loch\f77 41.\tab}}\pard \ltrpar\ql \fi-360\li2160\ri0\sb100\sa100\sbauto1\saauto1\widctlpar
\jclisttab\tx720\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\ls41\adjustright\rin0\lin2160\itap0\pararsid14899619 {\rtlch \ai\af0\afs20 \ltrch \i\f77\fs20\cf2\insrsid14899619 ({\*\bkmkstart n41}}{\field\fldedit{\*\fldinst {\rtlch \ai\af0\afs20 \ltrch 
\i\f77\fs20\cf2\insrsid14899619  HYPERLINK "http://www.sichosinenglish.org/books/upsherinish/03.htm" \\l "t41" }}{\fldrslt {\rtlch \ai\af0\afs20 \ltrch \cs16\i\f77\fs20\ul\cf6\insrsid14899619 Back to text}}}{\rtlch \ai\af0\afs20 \ltrch 
\i\f77\fs20\cf2\insrsid14899619 {\*\bkmkend n41}) There is no difficulty with giving women a 
chance to participate in this practice (see Kores Itim, pp. 69-70; Ziv Minhagim, p. 105). (Needless to say, the men and the women should not mix, but the child may be brought to the place where the women are congregating so that they can also cut off a po
rtion of his hair.) Indeed, certain authorities advise the mother to cut off some hair. Since she has a responsibility in educating the child, she should take part in the ceremony initiating his education.
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\ltrpar \rtlch \ai\af0\afs20\alang1025 \ltrch \i\f77\fs20\cf2\insrsid14899619 \hich\af77\dbch\af0\loch\f77 42.\tab}}\pard \ltrpar\ql \fi-360\li2160\ri0\sb100\sa100\sbauto1\saauto1\widctlpar
\jclisttab\tx720\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\ls42\adjustright\rin0\lin2160\itap0\pararsid14899619 {\rtlch \ai\af0\afs20 \ltrch \i\f77\fs20\cf2\insrsid14899619 ({\*\bkmkstart n42}}{\field\fldedit{\*\fldinst {\rtlch \ai\af0\afs20 \ltrch 
\i\f77\fs20\cf2\insrsid14899619  HYPERLINK "http://www.sichosinenglish.org/books/upsherinish/03.htm" \\l "t42" }}{\fldrslt {\rtlch \ai\af0\afs20 \ltrch \cs16\i\f77\fs20\ul\cf6\insrsid14899619 Back to text}}}{\rtlch \ai\af0\afs20 \ltrch 
\i\f77\fs20\cf2\insrsid14899619 {\*\bkmkend n42}) S'dei Chemed, Asifas Dinim, Chol HaMoed, sec. 5).
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\ltrpar \rtlch \ai\af0\afs20\alang1025 \ltrch \i\f77\fs20\cf2\insrsid14899619 \hich\af77\dbch\af0\loch\f77 43.\tab}}\pard \ltrpar\ql \fi-360\li2160\ri0\sb100\sa100\sbauto1\saauto1\widctlpar
\jclisttab\tx720\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\ls43\adjustright\rin0\lin2160\itap0\pararsid14899619 {\rtlch \ai\af0\afs20 \ltrch \i\f77\fs20\cf2\insrsid14899619 ({\*\bkmkstart n43}}{\field\fldedit{\*\fldinst {\rtlch \ai\af0\afs20 \ltrch 
\i\f77\fs20\cf2\insrsid14899619  HYPERLINK "http://www.sichosinenglish.org/books/upsherinish/03.htm" \\l "t43" }}{\fldrslt {\rtlch \ai\af0\afs20 \ltrch \cs16\i\f77\fs20\ul\cf6\insrsid14899619 Back to text}}}{\rtlch \ai\af0\afs20 \ltrch 
\i\f77\fs20\cf2\insrsid14899619 {\*\bkmkend n43}) Others including the Skleneler Rebbe and the chassid, R. Itchah, the Masmid, would begin cutting at the place where ultimately the child would put on tefillin.
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\ltrpar \rtlch \ai\af0\afs20\alang1025 \ltrch \i\f77\fs20\cf2\insrsid14899619 \hich\af77\dbch\af0\loch\f77 44.\tab}}\pard \ltrpar\ql \fi-360\li2160\ri0\sb100\sa100\sbauto1\saauto1\widctlpar
