\i\f77\fs20\cf2\insrsid14899619 {\*\bkmkend n47}) See Shaarei Yerushalayim, p. 47.
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid14899619 {\rtlch \ai\af0\afs20 \ltrch \i\f77\fs20\cf2\lbr3\insrsid14899619 \line }{\rtlch \af0 \ltrch \insrsid14899619 
\par }{\rtlch \ab\af1\afs27 \ltrch \b\f1\fs27\cf2\insrsid14899619 Days On Which An Upsherinish Should Be Postponed
\par 
\par }{\rtlch \af0\afs20 \ltrch \f77\fs20\insrsid14899619 As mentioned above, the Rebbe placed a great emphasis on holding the upsherin
ish on the date of the child's third birthday, not before and not afterwards. Nevertheless, there are occasions when - because it is prohibited or customary not to cut hair - the upsherinish should be postponed. They include:}{\rtlch \af0 \ltrch 
\insrsid14899619 
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\ltrpar \rtlch \af0\afs20\alang1025 \ltrch \f77\fs20\insrsid14899619 \hich\af77\dbch\af0\loch\f77 a.\tab}}\pard \ltrpar\ql \fi-360\li1440\ri0\sb100\sa100\sbauto1\saauto1\widctlpar
\jclisttab\tx720\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\ls48\adjustright\rin0\lin1440\itap0\pararsid14899619 {\rtlch \af0\afs20 \ltrch \f77\fs20\insrsid14899619 Shabbos and festivals. The Rebbe writes}{\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \f77\fs15\insrsid14899619 [{\*\bkmkstart t48
}}{\field\fldedit{\*\fldinst {\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \f77\fs15\insrsid14899619  HYPERLINK "http://www.sichosinenglish.org/books/upsherinish/04.htm" \\l "n48" }}{\fldrslt {\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \cs16\f77\fs15\ul\cf2\insrsid14899619 48}}}{\rtlch 
\af0\afs15 \ltrch \f77\fs15\insrsid14899619 {\*\bkmkend t48}]}{\rtlch \af0\afs20 \ltrch \f77\fs20\insrsid14899619  the upsherinish should be held directly after the holy day, but not before.}{\rtlch \af0 \ltrch \insrsid14899619 
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\ltrpar \rtlch \af0\afs20\alang1025 \ltrch \f77\fs20\insrsid14899619 \hich\af77\dbch\af0\loch\f77 b.\tab}}{\rtlch \af0\afs20 \ltrch \f77\fs20\insrsid14899619 
Sefiras HaOmer, the Counting of the Omer. If the child's birthday is before Lag BaOme
r, the Rebbe writes that one could find rationales to allow the upsherinish to be held during the Counting of the Omer, although generally haircuts are not taken at this time. Nevertheless, since it is customary for children's hair to be cut on Lag BaOmer
, the upsherinish should be held at that time.}{\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \f77\fs15\insrsid14899619 [{\*\bkmkstart t49}}{\field\fldedit{\*\fldinst {\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \f77\fs15\insrsid14899619 
 HYPERLINK "http://www.sichosinenglish.org/books/upsherinish/04.htm" \\l "n49" }}{\fldrslt {\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \cs16\f77\fs15\ul\cf2\insrsid14899619 49}}}{\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \f77\fs15\insrsid14899619 {\*\bkmkend t49}]}{\rtlch \af0 \ltrch 
\insrsid14899619 
\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\s15\ql \li720\ri0\sb100\sa100\sbauto1\saauto1\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin720\itap0\pararsid14899619 \rtlch \af0\afs24\alang1025 \ltrch \fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch 
\af0\afs20 \ltrch \f77\fs20\insrsid14899619 If the child's birthday is after Lag BaOmer, the upsherinish should be held on the day preceding Shavuos.}{\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \f77\fs15\insrsid14899619 [{\*\bkmkstart t50}}{\field\fldedit{\*\fldinst {
\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \f77\fs15\insrsid14899619  HYPERLINK "http://www.sichosinenglish.org/books/upsherinish/04.htm" \\l "n50" }}{\fldrslt {\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \cs16\f77\fs15\ul\cf2\insrsid14899619 50}}}{\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch 
\f77\fs15\insrsid14899619 {\*\bkmkend t50}]}{\rtlch \af0 \ltrch \insrsid14899619 
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\ltrpar \rtlch \af0\afs20\alang1025 \ltrch \f77\fs20\insrsid14899619 \hich\af77\dbch\af0\loch\f77 c.\tab}}\pard\plain \ltrpar\ql \fi-360\li1440\ri0\sb100\sa100\sbauto1\saauto1\widctlpar
\jclisttab\tx720\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\ls48\adjustright\rin0\lin1440\itap0\pararsid14899619 \rtlch \af0\afs24\alang1025 \ltrch \fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch \af0\afs20 \ltrch \f77\fs20\insrsid14899619 
Bein HaMetzarim, the Three Weeks between Tammuz 17 and Tishah BeAv - It is also customary not to take haircuts during this time. The Rebbe writes}{\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \f77\fs15\insrsid14899619 [{\*\bkmkstart t51}}{\field\fldedit{\*\fldinst {\rtlch 
\af0\afs15 \ltrch \f77\fs15\insrsid14899619  HYPERLINK "http://www.sichosinenglish.org/books/upsherinish/04.htm" \\l "n51" }}{\fldrslt {\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \cs16\f77\fs15\ul\cf2\insrsid14899619 51}}}{\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch 
\f77\fs15\insrsid14899619 {\*\bkmkend t51}]}{\rtlch \af0\afs20 \ltrch \f77\fs20\insrsid14899619  that if a child's birthday is between Rosh Chodesh Av and Tishah BeAv, the upsherinish should be held after the fast day.}{\rtlch \af0 \ltrch 
\insrsid14899619 
\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\s15\ql \li720\ri0\sb100\sa100\sbauto1\saauto1\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin720\itap0\pararsid14899619 \rtlch \af0\afs24\alang1025 \ltrch \fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch 
\af0\afs20 \ltrch \f77\fs20\insrsid14899619 With regard to a child whose birthday is between Tammuz 17 and Rosh Chodesh Av, we find a dif
ference of opinion among the later halachic authorities. Kapos Temarim (sec. 14) states that the upsherinish should be postponed until after Tishah BeAv. Toras Yekusial (Responsum 47), by contrast, rules that the upsherinish should be held on the child's 
birthday.}{\rtlch \af0 \ltrch \insrsid14899619 
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\ltrpar \rtlch \af0\afs20\alang1025 \ltrch \f77\fs20\insrsid14899619 \hich\af77\dbch\af0\loch\f77 d.\tab}}\pard\plain \ltrpar\ql \fi-360\li1440\ri0\sb100\sa100\sbauto1\saauto1\widctlpar
\jclisttab\tx720\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\ls48\adjustright\rin0\lin1440\itap0\pararsid14899619 \rtlch \af0\afs24\alang1025 \ltrch \fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch \af0\afs20 \ltrch \f77\fs20\insrsid14899619 
Rosh Chodesh - Rav Yehudah HaChossid}{\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \f77\fs15\insrsid14899619 [{\*\bkmkstart t52}}{\field\fldedit{\*\fldinst {\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \f77\fs15\insrsid14899619 
 HYPERLINK "http://www.sichosinenglish.org/books/upsherinish/04.htm" \\l "n52" }}{\fldrslt {\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \cs16\f77\fs15\ul\cf2\insrsid14899619 52}}}{\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \f77\fs15\insrsid14899619 {\*\bkmkend t52}]}{\rtlch \af0\afs20 
\ltrch \f77\fs20\insrsid14899619  advised that a person should not take a haircut on Rosh Chodesh. The Rebbe writes}{\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \f77\fs15\insrsid14899619 [{\*\bkmkstart t53}}{\field\fldedit{\*\fldinst {\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch 
\f77\fs15\insrsid14899619  HYPERLINK "http://www.sichosinenglish.org/books/upsherinish/04.htm" \\l "n53" }}{\fldrslt {\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \cs16\f77\fs15\ul\cf2\insrsid14899619 53}}}{\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \f77\fs15\insrsid14899619 {\*\bkmkend t53}]
}{\rtlch \af0\afs20 \ltrch \f77\fs20\insrsid14899619 
 that a distinction could be made between a child's first haircut - which fulfills a significant Jewish custom - and an ordinary haircut. Nevertheless, since an upsherinish is not an actual mitzvah, it is proper to postpone it until after Rosh Chodesh.}{
\rtlch \af0 \ltrch \insrsid14899619 
