\par {\listtext\pard\plain\ltrpar \rtlch \ai\af0\afs20\alang1025 \ltrch \i\f77\fs20\cf2\insrsid14899619 \hich\af77\dbch\af0\loch\f77 62.\tab}}\pard \ltrpar\ql \fi-360\li2160\ri0\sb100\sa100\sbauto1\saauto1\widctlpar
\jclisttab\tx720\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\ls63\adjustright\rin0\lin2160\itap0\pararsid14899619 {\rtlch \ai\af0\afs20 \ltrch \i\f77\fs20\cf2\insrsid14899619 ({\*\bkmkstart n62}}{\field\fldedit{\*\fldinst {\rtlch \ai\af0\afs20 \ltrch 
\i\f77\fs20\cf2\insrsid14899619  HYPERLINK "http://www.sichosinenglish.org/books/upsherinish/05.htm" \\l "t62" }}{\fldrslt {\rtlch \ai\af0\afs20 \ltrch \cs16\i\f77\fs20\ul\cf6\insrsid14899619 Back to text}}}{\rtlch \ai\af0\afs20 \ltrch 
\i\f77\fs20\cf2\insrsid14899619 {\*\bkmkend n62}) Igros Kodesh, Vol. XX, p. 10.
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid14899619 {\rtlch \ai\af0\afs20 \ltrch \i\f77\fs20\cf2\lbr3\insrsid14899619 \line }{\rtlch \af0 \ltrch \insrsid14899619 
\par }{\rtlch \ab\af1\afs27 \ltrch \b\f1\fs27\cf2\insrsid14899619 Areinfirinish - A Child's Entry Into Cheder
\par 
\par }{\rtlch \af0\afs20 \ltrch \f77\fs20\insrsid14899619 In Hilchos Talmud Torah 1:1, the Alter Rebbe writes:}{\rtlch \af0 \ltrch \insrsid14899619 
\par }{\rtlch \ai\af0\afs20 \ltrch \i\f77\fs20\insrsid14899619 When is a father obligated to begin teaching his son [verses from the Torah]? When [the son] knows how to speak. He should teach him the verses: Torah Tzivah Lanu Moshe and Shema Yisrael.}{\rtlch 
\af0 \ltrch \insrsid14899619 
\par }{\rtlch \af0\afs20 \ltrch \f77\fs20\insrsid14899619 As a child progresses, after hi
s parents teach him at home for a certain time, he is taken to a cheder to study under a teacher. Although there is no specific age stated when this should be done, it is common practice in certain communities to begin at the age of three, on the day of o
r shortly after the upsherinish. In one of his letters, the Rebbe}{\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \f77\fs15\insrsid14899619 [{\*\bkmkstart t63}}{\field\fldedit{\*\fldinst {\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \f77\fs15\insrsid14899619 
 HYPERLINK "http://www.sichosinenglish.org/books/upsherinish/06.htm" \\l "n63" }}{\fldrslt {\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \cs16\f77\fs15\ul\cf2\insrsid14899619 63}}}{\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \f77\fs15\insrsid14899619 {\*\bkmkend t63}]}{\rtlch \af0\afs20 
\ltrch \f77\fs20\insrsid14899619  writes that if parents educate a child at home, they need not rush to send him to cheder before the age of three. Similarly, if the common custom in a community is to begin cheder}{\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch 
\f77\fs15\insrsid14899619 [{\*\bkmkstart t64}}{\field\fldedit{\*\fldinst {\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \f77\fs15\insrsid14899619  HYPERLINK "http://www.sichosinenglish.org/books/upsherinish/06.htm" \\l "n64" }}{\fldrslt {\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch 
\cs16\f77\fs15\ul\cf2\insrsid14899619 64}}}{\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \f77\fs15\insrsid14899619 {\*\bkmkend t64}]}{\rtlch \af0\afs20 \ltrch \f77\fs20\insrsid14899619  somewhat later, the beginning of the child's formal study may be delayed until that time.
}{\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \f77\fs15\insrsid14899619 [{\*\bkmkstart t65}}{\field\fldedit{\*\fldinst {\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \f77\fs15\insrsid14899619  HYPERLINK "http://www.sichosinenglish.org/books/upsherinish/06.htm" \\l "n65" }}{\fldrslt {\rtlch 
\af0\afs15 \ltrch \cs16\f77\fs15\ul\cf2\insrsid14899619 65}}}{\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \f77\fs15\insrsid14899619 {\*\bkmkend t65}]}{\rtlch \af0 \ltrch \insrsid14899619 
\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\s3\qc \li0\ri0\sb100\sa100\sbauto1\saauto1\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel2\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid14899619 \rtlch \ab\af0\afs27\alang1025 \ltrch \b\fs27\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {
\rtlch \af0\afs20 \ltrch \f77\fs20\cf2\insrsid14899619 The Order of The Areinfirinish}{\rtlch \af0 \ltrch \insrsid14899619 
\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid14899619 \rtlch \af0\afs24\alang1025 \ltrch \fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch \af0\afs20 \ltrch \f77\fs20\insrsid14899619 
The customs for the areinfirinish to follow are based on the portion Hachnasah L'Beis HaMelamed in the Siddur of Rav Yaakov Emden and the description of the Tzemach Tzedek's areinfirinish in Sefer HaSichos 5700.}{\rtlch \af0 \ltrch \insrsid14899619 

\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\s15\ql \li0\ri0\sb100\sa100\sbauto1\saauto1\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid14899619 \rtlch \af0\afs24\alang1025 \ltrch \fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch \af0\afs20 
\ltrch \f77\fs20\insrsid14899619 In the morning, the father takes his child to the cheder wrapped in a tallis,}{\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \f77\fs15\insrsid14899619 [{\*\bkmkstart t66}}{\field\fldedit{\*\fldinst {\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch 
\f77\fs15\insrsid14899619  HYPERLINK "http://www.sichosinenglish.org/books/upsherinish/06.htm" \\l "n66" }}{\fldrslt {\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \cs16\f77\fs15\ul\cf2\insrsid14899619 66}}}{\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \f77\fs15\insrsid14899619 {\*\bkmkend t66}]
}{\rtlch \af0\afs20 \ltrch \f77\fs20\insrsid14899619  so that he should not see anything impure.}{\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \f77\fs15\insrsid14899619 [{\*\bkmkstart t67}}{\field\fldedit{\*\fldinst {\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \f77\fs15\insrsid14899619 
 HYPERLINK "http://www.sichosinenglish.org/books/upsherinish/06.htm" \\l "n67" }}{\fldrslt {\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \cs16\f77\fs15\ul\cf2\insrsid14899619 67}}}{\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \f77\fs15\insrsid14899619 {\*\bkmkend t67}]}{\rtlch \af0\afs20 
\ltrch \f77\fs20\insrsid14899619  This also trains him in the practice of modesty and protects him from the evil eye.}{\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \f77\fs15\insrsid14899619 [{\*\bkmkstart t68}}{\field\fldedit{\*\fldinst {\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch 
\f77\fs15\insrsid14899619  HYPERLINK "http://www.sichosinenglish.org/books/upsherinish/06.htm" \\l "n68" }}{\fldrslt {\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \cs16\f77\fs15\ul\cf2\insrsid14899619 68}}}{\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \f77\fs15\insrsid14899619 {\*\bkmkend t68}]
}{\rtlch \af0\afs20 \ltrch \f77\fs20\insrsid14899619  After entering the cheder, the child is taken out from the tallis and it is then draped around his shoulders.}{\rtlch \af0 \ltrch \insrsid14899619 
\par }{\rtlch \af0\afs20 \ltrch \f77\fs20\insrsid14899619 The teacher seats the child on his lap}{\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \f77\fs15\insrsid14899619 [{\*\bkmkstart t69}}{\field\fldedit{\*\fldinst {\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \f77\fs15\insrsid14899619 
 HYPERLINK "http://www.sichosinenglish.org/books/upsherinish/06.htm" \\l "n69" }}{\fldrslt {\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \cs16\f77\fs15\ul\cf2\insrsid14899619 69}}}{\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \f77\fs15\insrsid14899619 {\*\bkmkend t69}]}{\rtlch \af0\afs20 
\ltrch \f77\fs20\insrsid14899619  and begins teaching him the Alef Beis. It is customary to begin with the Alef from the title-page of the Tanya.}{\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \f77\fs15\insrsid14899619 [{\*\bkmkstart t70}}{\field\fldedit{\*\fldinst {\rtlch 
\af0\afs15 \ltrch \f77\fs15\insrsid14899619  HYPERLINK "http://www.sichosinenglish.org/books/upsherinish/06.htm" \\l "n70" }}{\fldrslt {\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \cs16\f77\fs15\ul\cf2\insrsid14899619 70}}}{\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch 
\f77\fs15\insrsid14899619 {\*\bkmkend t70}]}{\rtlch \af0\afs20 \ltrch \f77\fs20\insrsid14899619  The teacher points to the letter, says Alef, and the child repeats Alef. Using a toothpick,}{\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \f77\fs15\insrsid14899619 [
{\*\bkmkstart t71}}{\field\fldedit{\*\fldinst {\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \f77\fs15\insrsid14899619  HYPERLINK "http://www.sichosinenglish.org/books/upsherinish/06.htm" \\l "n71" }}{\fldrslt {\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \cs16\f77\fs15\ul\cf2\insrsid14899619 71
}}}{\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \f77\fs15\insrsid14899619 {\*\bkmkend t71}]}{\rtlch \af0\afs20 \ltrch \f77\fs20\insrsid14899619  the teacher coats the Alef with honey. The child recites the blessing Shehakol and then licks the honey.}{\rtlch \af0\afs15 
\ltrch \f77\fs15\insrsid14899619 [{\*\bkmkstart t72}}{\field\fldedit{\*\fldinst {\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \f77\fs15\insrsid14899619  HYPERLINK "http://www.sichosinenglish.org/books/upsherinish/06.htm" \\l "n72" }}{\fldrslt {\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch 
\cs16\f77\fs15\ul\cf2\insrsid14899619 72}}}{\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \f77\fs15\insrsid14899619 {\*\bkmkend t72}]}{\rtlch \af0 \ltrch \insrsid14899619 
\par }{\rtlch \af0\afs20 \ltrch \f77\fs20\insrsid14899619 
Afterwards, the teacher reads the Alef-Beis letter after letter for the child, pointing to the letters and having the child repeat after him. He then reads the letters in reverse order Suf-Shin-Reish, with the chi
ld repeating. He then teaches the child each of the nekudos (vowels), reading them in order and then in reverse order with the child repeating after him.}{\rtlch \af0 \ltrch \insrsid14899619 
\par }{\rtlch \af0\afs20 \ltrch \f77\fs20\insrsid14899619 The teacher then takes a Chumash Vayikra}{\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \f77\fs15\insrsid14899619 [{\*\bkmkstart t73}}{\field\fldedit{\*\fldinst {\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \f77\fs15\insrsid14899619 
 HYPERLINK "http://www.sichosinenglish.org/books/upsherinish/06.htm" \\l "n73" }}{\fldrslt {\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \cs16\f77\fs15\ul\cf2\insrsid14899619 73}}}{\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \f77\fs15\insrsid14899619 {\*\bkmkend t73}]}{\rtlch \af0\afs20 
\ltrch \f77\fs20\insrsid14899619  and reads the first few verses.}{\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \f77\fs15\insrsid14899619 [{\*\bkmkstart t74}}{\field\fldedit{\*\fldinst {\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \f77\fs15\insrsid14899619 
 HYPERLINK "http://www.sichosinenglish.org/books/upsherinish/06.htm" \\l "n74" }}{\fldrslt {\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \cs16\f77\fs15\ul\cf2\insrsid14899619 74}}}{\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \f77\fs15\insrsid14899619 {\*\bkmkend t74}]}{\rtlch \af0\afs20 
\ltrch \f77\fs20\insrsid14899619  The child should repeat after the teacher word after word.}{\rtlch \af0 \ltrch \insrsid14899619 
\par }{\rtlch \af0\afs20 \ltrch \f77\fs20\insrsid14899619 The teacher then recites - and the child repeats - the verse: }{\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \f77\fs15\insrsid14899619 [{\*\bkmkstart t75}}{\field\fldedit{\*\fldinst {\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch 
\f77\fs15\insrsid14899619  HYPERLINK "http://www.sichosinenglish.org/books/upsherinish/06.htm" \\l "n75" }}{\fldrslt {\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \cs16\f77\fs15\ul\cf2\insrsid14899619 75}}}{\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \f77\fs15\insrsid14899619 {\*\bkmkend t75}]
}{\rtlch \af0\afs20 \ltrch \f77\fs20\insrsid14899619  Torah Tzivah Lanu Moshe Morasha Kehilas Yaakov, "The Torah which Moshe commanded us is the heritage of the congregation of Jacob" and the request Torah Tehai Emunos
i Ve-Eil Shadai Be'ezras, "May the Torah be my faith and may the A-lmighty G-d be my succor."}{\rtlch \af0 \ltrch \insrsid14899619 
\par }{\rtlch \af0\afs20 \ltrch \f77\fs20\insrsid14899619 The parents give the teacher a honey cake,}{\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \f77\fs15\insrsid14899619 [{\*\bkmkstart t76}}{\field\fldedit{\*\fldinst {\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \f77\fs15\insrsid14899619 
 HYPERLINK "http://www.sichosinenglish.org/books/upsherinish/06.htm" \\l "n76" }}{\fldrslt {\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \cs16\f77\fs15\ul\cf2\insrsid14899619 76}}}{\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \f77\fs15\insrsid14899619 {\*\bkmkend t76}]}{\rtlch \af0\afs20 
\ltrch \f77\fs20\insrsid14899619  cooked in oil,}{\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \f77\fs15\insrsid14899619 [{\*\bkmkstart t77}}{\field\fldedit{\*\fldinst {\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \f77\fs15\insrsid14899619  HYPERLINK "http:/
/www.sichosinenglish.org/books/upsherinish/06.htm" \\l "n77" }}{\fldrslt {\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \cs16\f77\fs15\ul\cf2\insrsid14899619 77}}}{\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \f77\fs15\insrsid14899619 {\*\bkmkend t77}]}{\rtlch \af0\afs20 \ltrch 
\f77\fs20\insrsid14899619  on which the following verses have been inscribed: }{\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \f77\fs15\insrsid14899619 [{\*\bkmkstart t78}}{\field\fldedit{\*\fldinst {\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \f77\fs15\insrsid14899619 
 HYPERLINK "http://www.sichosinenglish.org/books/upsherinish/06.htm" \\l "n78" }}{\fldrslt {\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \cs16\f77\fs15\ul\cf2\insrsid14899619 78}}}{\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \f77\fs15\insrsid14899619 {\*\bkmkend t78}]}{\rtlch \af0\afs20 
\ltrch \f77\fs20\insrsid14899619  "G-d, the L-rd, has granted me a tongue of instructio
n to appreciate the need of the times, to teach those thirsty for the word [of G-d]. He arouses me morning after morning. He spurs my ear to hear as one would the students. G-d, the L-rd, has opened my ear; I did not rebel. I did not withdraw to the rear.
" The teacher reads the verses and the child repeats after him word for word. The teacher then removes the inscriptions and gives the cake to the boy, who eats it after reciting the blessing borei minei mezonos.}{\rtlch \af0 \ltrch \insrsid14899619 

\par }{\rtlch \af0\afs20 \ltrch \f77\fs20\insrsid14899619 The child is then given a shelled hard-boiled egg upon which the following verse has been written: }{\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \f77\fs15\insrsid14899619 [{\*\bkmkstart t79}}{\field\fldedit{\*\fldinst {
\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \f77\fs15\insrsid14899619  HYPERLINK "http://www.sichosinenglish.org/books/upsherinish/06.htm" \\l "n79" }}{\fldrslt {\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \cs16\f77\fs15\ul\cf2\insrsid14899619 79}}}{\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch 
\f77\fs15\insrsid14899619 {\*\bkmkend t79}]}{\rtlch \af0\afs20 \ltrch \f77\fs20\insrsid14899619  "And he said to me: 'Son of man, feed your stomach and fill your gut with this scroll which I will give you.' I ate,
 and it was as sweet as honey in my mouth."}{\rtlch \af0 \ltrch \insrsid14899619 
\par }{\rtlch \af0\afs20 \ltrch \f77\fs20\insrsid14899619 Again, the teacher reads the verses and the child repeats after him word for word. The child then eats the egg.}{\rtlch \af0 \ltrch \insrsid14899619 
\par }{\rtlch \af0\afs20 \ltrch \f77\fs20\insrsid14899619 The child gives generously to tzedakah.}{\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \f77\fs15\insrsid14899619 [{\*\bkmkstart t80}}{\field\fldedit{\*\fldinst {\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \f77\fs15\insrsid14899619 
 HYPERLINK "http://www.sichosinenglish.org/books/upsherinish/06.htm" \\l "n80" }}{\fldrslt {\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \cs16\f77\fs15\ul\cf2\insrsid14899619 80}}}{\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \f77\fs15\insrsid14899619 {\*\bkmkend t80}]}{\rtlch \af0\afs20 
\ltrch \f77\fs20\insrsid14899619  Candies are thrown upon the child and he is told that they were thrown by the Angel Michoel.}{\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \f77\fs15\insrsid14899619 [{\*\bkmkstart t81}}{\field\fldedit{\*\fldinst {\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch 
\f77\fs15\insrsid14899619  HYPERLINK "http://www.sichosinenglish.org/books/upsherinish/06.htm" \\l "n81" }}{\fldrslt {\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \cs16\f77\fs15\ul\cf2\insrsid14899619 81}}}{\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \f77\fs15\insrsid14899619 {\*\bkmkend t81}]
}{\rtlch \af0\afs20 \ltrch \f77\fs20\insrsid14899619  The child also distributes bags of candies to the other children.}{\rtlch \af0 \ltrch \insrsid14899619 
\par }{\rtlch \af0\afs20 \ltrch \f77\fs20\insrsid14899619 In the evening, it is customary for the family to hold a celebratory feast.}{\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \f77\fs15\insrsid14899619 [{\*\bkmkstart t82}}{\field\fldedit{\*\fldinst {\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch 
\f77\fs15\insrsid14899619  HYPERLINK "http://www.sichosinenglish.org/books/upsherinish/06.htm" \\l "n82" }}{\fldrslt {\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \cs16\f77\fs15\ul\cf2\insrsid14899619 82}}}{\rtlch \af0\afs15 \ltrch \f77\fs15\insrsid14899619 {\*\bkmkend t82}]
}{\rtlch \af0 \ltrch \insrsid14899619 
\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\qc \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid14899619 \rtlch \af0\afs24\alang1025 \ltrch \fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\field\fldedit{\*\fldinst {\rtlch \af0\afs20 \ltrch 
